  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 931 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge is forecast to slight shift to the west the\nbegin the week, allowing relatively (key word here) cooler\ntemperatures to settle over the TN Valley. High temperatures will\nstill be in the low 90s with overnight lows in the mid 60s to low 70s\nas Moderate (level 2 of 4) heat impacts continue through the week. As\nthe ridge shifts back eastward, temperatures will gradually climb\nback into the mid 90s by the end of the week with diurnal heating\ncontributing to low chances (20% or less) of thunderstorm development\neach day. One thing to watch will be where sfc high pressure sets up\nalong the Appalachians and whether or not NE AL and southern middle\nTN experience CAD (cold used loosely). If this is the case, increased\nPoPs may be necessary as differential heating boundaries begin to set\nup along North Central AL. As far as heat headlines go, will likely\nnot need anything past Sunday as heat indices drop to around 100\ndegrees.",
